# Backend rules

## App entry

`backend/server.py` — FastAPI with `/api` router prefix.

## Endpoints

- `GET /api/` — liveness
- `POST /api/contact` — lead form (Pydantic `ContactFormRequest`)
- `GET /api/status` — MongoDB status checks (legacy)

## Contact + email

- Validate with Pydantic (`EmailStr` for email)
- Send email via `background_tasks.add_task(send_contact_email, ...)`
- Never block HTTP response on SendGrid latency
- `reply_to` = submitter email
- Env: `SENDGRID_API_KEY`, `SENDER_EMAIL`, `RECIPIENT_EMAIL`

## Style

- Async route handlers
- Log errors with `logging`; return generic 500 messages to clients
- Do not re-enable MongoDB contact persistence without approval
- CORS from `CORS_ORIGINS` env (comma-separated)

## Testing

After API changes, run `python backend_test.py` from repo root.
